---
import PageContainer from '../components/layout/PageContainer.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = false;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About LUDWISE — LUDWISE"
  description="What LUDWISE is, who operates it, and how its game and store information works."
  activeNavId="about"
>
  <PageContainer width="reading">
    <article class="lw-about">
      <h1 class="lw-text-heading-xl">About LUDWISE</h1>
      <p class="lw-text-body-lg">
        LUDWISE is a public PC game discovery and store-information project operated by Daniel
        Kindl.
      </p>

      <h2 class="lw-text-heading-md">What it does</h2>
      <p class="lw-text-body-md">
        LUDWISE brings game information, store offers, prices, and observed price history into one
        interface. The MVP starts with Steam as its first store. More stores can be added later.
      </p>
      <p class="lw-text-body-md">
        The site does not sell games. When you choose an offer, LUDWISE sends you to the store where
        the purchase can take place.
      </p>

      <h2 class="lw-text-heading-md">Where the information comes from</h2>
      <p class="lw-text-body-md">
        Game information comes from IGDB. Store offers and prices come from Steam. LUDWISE also
        creates some presentation values from provider observations, such as freshness information.
        The site identifies source data and derived information where that distinction matters.
      </p>
      <p class="lw-text-body-md">
        See <a href="/legal/sources">Data sources</a> for provider attribution and more detail.
      </p>

      <h2 class="lw-text-heading-md">How the MVP is funded</h2>
      <p class="lw-text-body-md">
        The public MVP has no advertising, affiliate links, subscriptions, or payments. Store order
        is not influenced by a commercial relationship.
      </p>

      <h2 class="lw-text-heading-md">Privacy and contact</h2>
      <p class="lw-text-body-md">
        LUDWISE runs no product analytics at launch. The public policies describe the limited
        technical data needed to serve and operate the site.
      </p>
      <p class="lw-text-body-md">
        Read the <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> or use the{' '}
        <a href="/legal/contact">Contact</a> page to reach the operator.
      </p>

      <h2 class="lw-text-heading-md">Source code</h2>
      <p class="lw-text-body-md">
        The web interface is open source. You can inspect it in the{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/ludwise/ludwise-web">LUDWISE web repository</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </PageContainer>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lw-about > * + * {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-4);
  }

  .lw-about h2 {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-8);
  }
</style>
